    "body": "## Security impact\n\nThe exact-location and exact-route endpoints are the highest-sensitivity job read surfaces because they can return precise coordinates, private address labels, route stops and route geometry. They still loaded a job globally by numeric `jobId` before checking whether the authenticated caller was the requester or assigned worker.\n\nThat allowed an authenticated outsider to distinguish a nonexistent job (`404`) from an existing private job (`403`) even after the job had disappeared from public discovery/detail, creating an existence oracle over private job activity through location-sensitive endpoints.\n\n## Fix\n\n- resolve exact location/route access through the existing participant-scoped `JobRepository.findParticipantById(jobId, userId)` query before reading exact location data or evaluating lifecycle state;\n- return the existing generic exact-location `403` for missing identity, nonexistent IDs and non-participants, making those cases indistinguishable to outsiders;\n- preserve participant lifecycle rules: requester can inspect exact location while the job is open, requester/assigned worker can inspect it for active accepted/disputed jobs, and exact location remains unavailable after completion/cancellation;\n- preserve the established runtime API contract for outsiders (`403`) rather than weakening or reshaping it.\n\nNo coordinate storage, private-label retention, route geometry, tracking, settlement, escrow or financial logic is changed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- add focused regression coverage proving outsider exact-location and exact-route access goes only through participant-scoped lookup;\n- prove missing authenticated identity fails closed before repository access;\n- preserve requester access before assignment and during an active/disputed job;\n- preserve terminal lifecycle denial for requester/worker;\n- update existing full-route and multi-stop tests to exercise the participant-scoped lookup rather than the former global lookup.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all relevant checks on the exact PR head are green, revalidate that `master` has not moved (or safely rebase if it has), then merge with a merge commit using the exact checked head SHA. Verify the resulting master commit and all post-merge workflows before starting another slice.",
